                                                "sense_id": "831498f5-80b3-30a5-b3aa-5a6903fefa2c",
                                                "text": "He would listen quietly at meetings of the Politburo, or to distinguished visitors, puffing at his Dunhill pipe, doodling aimlessly - his secretaries Poskrebyshev and Dvinsky write that his pads were sometimes covered with the phrase ‘Lenin-teacher-friend’, but the last foreigner to visit him, in February 1953, noted that he was doodling wolves."
                                            }
                                        ]
